WEBVTT

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.030
<b>Skull-face Bookseller Honda-san</b>

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:06.040
<i>To all of you bookstore lovers out 
there in the 47 prefectures of Japan...</i>

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.050
<i>Have you ever seen anyone 
like this at a shop?</i>

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.250
<i>Men and women in suits, looking 
intently through the store</i>

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:17.990
<b>P Company</b>

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.560
<i>with a paper bag or stack 
of papers in their hands.</i>

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:19.690
There he is!

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:20.910
Honda-san!

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:23.440
I thought I asked you to put the posters up!

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.280
I told you there's no room!

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.530
<i>They're highly likely to be salespeople 
from a publishing company.</i>

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.240
<b>A Battle Without Honor or Humanity</b>

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:38.700
<i>Salespeople are the people 
from publishing companies</i>

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.910
<i>that travel to bookstores 
to sell their books.</i>

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.420
Honda-san.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:45.480
We apologize for the confusion 
regarding the posters.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.350
We confronted you without considering 
the trouble we were causing you.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.020
It's not so much "trouble" as
 it is "physically impossible."

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:56.970
We've come to the conclusion that
 we should consider our pitch first

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.730
and worry about the size of the poster later.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.690
So we made a ton in A5 size!

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.770
The pop-ups are laminated, too.

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:07.720
Please make good use of them!

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.270
<b>Accept 
Receive</b>

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:12.420
Okay.

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.210
<b>Be a bookstore that can say "NO!"</b>

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.490
Don't let them walk over you!

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.610
Okay...

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.140
You gotta say no if we don't need it.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.380
Don't you feel like you should put it up when
 salespeople tell you they made it by hand?

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:23.910
Weak!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.590
That's what I would be counting 
on if I were in sales.

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:33.360
<b>Sales</b>

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:32.980
<i>The giant paper bags that salespeople 
walk around with often contain signage.</i>

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.360
signage

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.790
<i>For example, pop-ups for 
catching the eye at the shop,</i>

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Pop-ups</b>

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.310
<i>flyers, sales displays, 
sample page pamphlets,</i>

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Flyers</b>

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Sales displays</b>

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Sample page pamphlets</b>

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:43.540
<i>and paper boards autographed by 
the authors, among other things.</i>

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:43.800
<b>Autographed paper boards</b>

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.760
<i>As I'm not very assertive,</i>

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.340
<b>Unassertive Bookstore</b>

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.710
<i>It's hard for me to refuse when they 
give me things they say are handmade.</i>

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:52.650
<i>Here's another thing that 
happens all the time.</i>

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.180
<b>One day...</b>

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:56.850
We're going to be releasing 
a special edition.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.850
<b>Special Edition</b>

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:58.620
Again?

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.820
So I'm wondering if you could stock a little 
more than usual for the first batch.

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:06.130
Okay, then...

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.180
Two copies.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:08.220
Tw—

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.280
Twenty copies!

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.310
Thank you!

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.680
We don't need that many.

00:03:12.680 --> 00:03:14.750
Who knows if we'll even sell two.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.070
Please!

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.790
Come on, please!

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.910
Please, help me!

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:23.980
Oh, I'm sorry, we're completely out, too.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.120
It's been selling like crazy 
since the ads went up!

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.510
Thank you.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:31.320
Hello.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:36.220
Section Chief Pestmask

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:33.970
This is Pestmask of ** Bookstore speaking.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:35.450
<i>Oh, hello.</i>

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.220
<i>I'm from the Sales—</i>

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:39.920
The bonus material for yesterday's 
comics arrived today, again.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:45.290
Obviously, we can't prepare unless the 
bonus material arrives before the comics.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.630
How many times have we discussed this?

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.790
Aren't you getting sick 
of this conversation?

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.500
<i>U-Um... Um...</i>

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.730
I will be awaiting a proposal for
 a meaningful resolution.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.100
<i>Y-Yes, ma'am! I'm sorry!</i>

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.640
There's all kinds of sales
 types out there.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.790
She sugarcoated it!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:07.380
To be honest, I want salespeople 
to bring books with them.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.400
Sometimes salespeople come 
without bringing the books we want.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.590
True.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.380
It was the Christmas 
season, a few years ago...

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:17.020
Around when that popular 
light novel first came out...

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.490
<b>Good job!</b>

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.490
Formerly in charge of light novels

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.550
Lantern-san, we don't have any 
more <i>I**egular</i> in stock, do we?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.450
A customer wants to reserve a copy.

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:26.090
Tell them there's no plans 
to restock, so we can't.

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.480
Lantern-san, someone from 
Kadokawa Sales is here.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.630
Well, hello.

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:33.040
<b>Kadokawa-dono</b>

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.040
Is <i>I**egular</i> selling well?

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:33.970
More, please!

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.430
I'm sorry, we're out!

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:36.850
Then why are you here?!

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.630
H-Hold on!

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.210
I don't have books, but we have these!

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.320
<b>Candy</b>

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:47.900
Merry Christmas, Lantern-san.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.450
Guys, Kadokawa's here.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:53.840
Whoa.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:54.660
All right!

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:58.220
It looks like they're talking to 
Koomote-chan about novels right now.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.240
Got it.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.330
I'll go when the time's right.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.610
Oh! There's something I'd like to talk to 
them about when Honda-san's done.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.240
I know, right?

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:13.050
We sell so many different books, we're 
a huge inconvenience to the bookstores.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:13.850
<b>Princess Kadokawa</b>

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:14.730
Um...

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.610
So you're in charge of, uh...

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.620
Art books.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.250
That's right!

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.770
Are there any books you need?

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.060
The <i>Psycho-P***</i> anime concept art book.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:27.250
Oh, is it selling?

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:28.270
Yay!

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:29.300
It is.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.300
Actually, it got bought 
out by a binge shopper.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:37.170
Give me all the P***o-Pass you've got.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.040
<i>Psycho-P***</i> has gone 
extinct from the shelves.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.170
That's hilarious!

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.810
Oh, no, not hilarious.

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.310
I'm grateful, yes.

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.280
A concept art book. Got it.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:43.160
Anything else?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:45.450
We're stocked up for the rest, so we're good.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.710
She's up next.

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:47.950
Kadokawa-san.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.950
Oh, hey, Section Chief Armor.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:54.050
We're all out of the BL book 
that came out yesterday. Help!

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:58.700
That's hysterical! Do you think
 it's all the same person?

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.160
Honda-san.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:00.480
Hello.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.960
Thank you for your help 
at the fair the other day.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.730
<i>It's him!</i>

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.460
Oh, hello.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:07.300
You're empty-handed.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.470
Oh, I was just passing by.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:12.270
<i>This man speaks fluent Japanese,</i>

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:15.900
<i>and is an industry insider who 
deserves to be known far and wide.</i>

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:25.180
Frédéric Toutlemonde-san (Voiced by: himself)

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.780
<i>Frédéric Toutlemonde-san.</i>

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:21.150
<i>He's an amazing person 
set on further spreading</i>

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.790
<i>the hugely popular bande dessinée comics.</i>

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:28.760
<i>There are two famous brands 
of bande dessinée,</i>

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:35.890
<b>Huma**ids</b>

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:35.890
Asu**shinsha

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:35.890
The two large bande dessinée brands

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:31.710
<i>and they each have different sellers.</i>

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:34.110
<i>Frédéric-san is the chief of both of them.</i>

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:35.630
<i>He's serious business.</i>

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:40.920
<i>An elite of the industry, filled 
with the passion of selling books.</i>

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.900
Say, Honda-san, about this manga...

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:49.910
<b>Shonen manga
 from France</b>

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:47.090
Is it all right if I quietly 
leave it next to <i>One P**ch Man</i>?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:49.720
<i>That's not for me to decide!</i>

00:06:52.310 --> 00:06:55.460
<i>There are no borders to salespeople's passion.</i>

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:59.160
<i>Today, once again, they
 give me plenty of energy.</i>

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:03.990
<b>Lost in Manga</b>

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:09.490
I want some good manga to read.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.680
I don't know, there's so many.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:15.220
I know what you mean.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:19.680
<i>They came into the bookstore 
looking for manga to read,</i>

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.870
<i>but there are so many options, 
they're at even more of a loss.</i>

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.260
<i>I've come up with a word for these people:</i>

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:31.450
<i>"Lost in Manga."</i>

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:35.180
Attention!

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.720
A moving shoujo manga.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.400
Three volumes at most.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.170
Interesting even for a man in his forties.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.130
How about the classic one-off, 
<i>The ***rt of Thomas</i>?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:51.430
I don't read too many shoujo manga, but 
how about <i>Shiota-***sei and Ama*-chan</i>?

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.650
Don't speak if you don't read shoujo.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.440
Wait, hear me out.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.150
What was it...

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:55.930
What was it...

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:57.250
That one that sold really well...

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:58.640
Oh, <i>Shiki no ***jitsu</i>.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:02.150
Thanks.

00:08:03.900 --> 00:08:05.560
What was that about?

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:07.480
Must have been a question from a customer.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:13.160
<i>It's not uncommon to see customers who 
ask, "Do you have any recommendations?"</i>

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:12.690
<b>See Episode 1</b>

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:16.010
<i>I, too, have one unforgettable experience.</i>

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:23.200
Look.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.270
Y-Yes?

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:29.540
This is my eleven-year-old granddaughter. 
She's eleven and French.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.530
<b>Audio</b>

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:29.530
<b>Japanese</b>

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:31.980
I'd like to buy her manga.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.020
I see.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.990
What kind of manga does she like?

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.140
Dunno.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:37.610
Dude!

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.470
Does your granddaughter
 understand Japanese?

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.670
Of course.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:45.620
She's interested in Japanese culture, 
and she can speak better than I can.

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.280
But she's not perfect.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.490
It'd be even better if she can 
read Japanese manga in French.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:53.590
I see.

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:59.030
Sorry, please just a moment.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:01.570
Save me!

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.940
Eleven-year-old French girl.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:04.100
Japanese-y manga.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:06.590
Preferably translated to French!

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.170
<i>Natsume **jincho</i>.

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:10.540
<i>U**na</i>! <i>No**me</i>! <i>Aka**ku</i>!

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:12.410
Hmm, <i>Chihaya**ru</i>?

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.350
I see!

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.620
Why <i>U**na</i> and <i>Aka**ku</i>?

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:16.520
Those are so old.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:17.870
She's eleven.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.730
Old or new, it doesn't matter.

00:09:20.730 --> 00:09:23.570
Be sure you check to make sure it's 
been translated before you tell him.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.420
Thank you very much!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.320
A bilingual version of <i>Chihaya**ru</i>?

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:29.060
<b>Western Books</b>

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:28.580
We have it!

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.460
Western Books

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:31.160
Bonsoir!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:32.810
Here you are!

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.540
All French... It's perfect!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.410
I'm so glad.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.380
My pleas—

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:46.950
<b>creak creak</b>

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:42.460
Merci.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.800
<i>I've never had such a powerful "merci."</i>

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:52.300
<i>Tracking down a customer's requests 
leads to a purchase of your choice.</i>

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:54.950
<i>It's quite a fun task,</i>

00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:59.190
<i>but I wonder if this is how 
people on quiz shows feel.</i>

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.310
Oh, Lantern-san.

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:05.960
How'd it go with the search for a shoujo manga 
that could entertain a man in his forties?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:11.120
That guy ended up buying <i>Berse*k</i>.

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.640
Male in
 his 40s

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.640
Shoujo

00:10:11.570 --> 00:10:14.640
Short

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.010
Y-You're kidding, right?

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:16.100
That's the exact opposite manga.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:20.140
<b>Changed his mind</b>

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:20.140
What was the point of asking for 
a manga that's three volumes tops?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.760
<i>Selling manga that the customer wants,</i>

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:25.160
<i>without being overwhelmed 
by the many strange turns...</i>

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.170
<i>That is the task of a comic bookstore.</i>
